/************************************************************************  TEMPLATE-DOC

 Liberty TEMPLATE for scripts/gen_cell_lib.py -- IHP SG13G2 (low-voltage devices).

 This whole comment block carries the marker TEMPLATE-DOC on its first line, which means
 gen_cell_lib.py strips it when rendering: it documents the template, and does not belong
 in the libraries generated from it.

 Everything outside the @TOKEN@ placeholders is copied through verbatim, so this file
 is where a technology's library-level constants live: units, delay/slew thresholds,
 wire-load models and the look-up-table templates.  The characterizer reads the units
 and the thresholds back out of the *filled* template and uses them both to place its
 ngspice .meas thresholds and to scale its SI measurements -- so retargeting the tool
 to another technology or another unit system is a matter of swapping this file.

 The values below are taken from the PDK's own libraries
 (libs.ref/sg13g2_stdcell/lib/sg13g2_stdcell_*.lib), so a library generated from this
 template can be read alongside them in one STA run without a unit or threshold clash.

 Required placeholders (gen_cell_lib.py refuses a template that is missing one):
   @LIBRARY_NAME@ @CELLS@ @VOLTAGE@ @TEMPERATURE@ @INDEX_SLEW@ @INDEX_LOAD@
 Optional placeholders (substituted when present):
   @PROCESS@ @OPCOND_NAME@ @DATE@ @GENCMD@ @COMMENT@
   @MAX_TRANSITION@ @MAX_CAPACITANCE@ @DEFAULT_INPUT_PIN_CAP@

 Copyright 2024 IHP PDK Authors (library constants)
 SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

************************************************************************/

